# fixedbugs, defect 2049, 2026-10-13, the defect's second reproducer.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own declaring `int
# h_<module>_main(int x);`, the name this compiler writes for the
# program's `main`, was told `internal error: compiling the generated C
# failed` at exit 2: clang's first error lies in the generated C, its note
# at the header's line.
#
# FIX: the header is refused at its line 3, exit 1, the name told as
# the one the C this compiler writes gives the program's `main`, with a
# `guess` fix renaming it in the header (`cli/declared_after.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-2049-a-header-that-declares-main-s-c-name-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
